# Files that belong to an upstream project are never committed here. They are
# staged into a task directory from the pinned fork under third_party/ by the
# adapter that owns the task, and regenerating them is one command:
#
#   python -m hv.adapters.airs generate --task <Name>
#   python -m hv.adapters.speedrun_pi stage
#
# The reason is licensing, not size. airs-bench is CC BY-NC 4.0, whose
# non-commercial term would otherwise attach to this repository; the Prime
# Intellect release carries no LICENSE at all, so nothing grants us the right to
# redistribute it. GitHub's terms do grant the right to fork both on GitHub,
# which is what third_party/ is.
#
# What stays committed is everything we wrote: task.toml, Dockerfiles, compose
# files, our verifiers, and reference solutions.

# AIRS: upstream's prepare/evaluate scripts, the gold labels they produce, and
# instruction.md — which is project_description.md verbatim plus the harness
# section the adapter appends, so it embeds upstream text either way.
airs/*/tests/upstream/
airs/*/tests/eval_data/
airs/*/instruction.md

# PI speedrun: program.md (as instruction.md) and the baseline training script.
# run.sh and verify.py are NOT here — they were never published, and ours are
# recovered from the tool results inside the released traces.
speedrun_pi/*/instruction.md
speedrun_pi/*/environment/train_gpt_simple.py
